#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:2
msgid "Read the Docs open source philosophy"
msgstr "Read the Docs 的开源理念"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:4
msgid ""
"Read the Docs is open source software. We have `licensed "
"<https://github.com/readthedocs/readthedocs.org/blob/main/LICENSE>`_ the "
"code base as MIT, which provides almost no restrictions on the use of the "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs 是开源软件。我们以 MIT 协议 `授权 "
"<https://github.com/readthedocs/readthedocs.org/blob/main/LICENSE>`_ "
"了整个代码库，该协议对代码使用几乎没有限制。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:8
msgid ""
"However, as a project there are things that we care about more than others. "
"We built Read the Docs to support documentation in the open source "
"community. The code is open for people to contribute to, so that they may "
"build features into https://app.readthedocs.org that they want. We also "
"believe sharing the code openly is a valuable learning tool, especially for "
"demonstrating how to collaborate and maintain an enormous website."
msgstr ""
"然而作为一个项目，我们有些东西比其他更重要。构建 Read the Docs 是为支持开源社区的文档。代码开放供人贡献，让人们可以把自己需要的功能构建进"
" https://app.readthedocs.org。我们也认为公开共享代码是有价值的学习工具，尤其能示范如何协作并维护一个庞大的网站。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:18
msgid "Official support"
msgstr "官方支持"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:20
msgid ""
"The time of the core developers of Read the Docs is limited. We provide "
"official support for the following things:"
msgstr "Read the Docs 核心开发者的时间有限。我们对以下事项提供官方支持："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:23
msgid "Local development on the Python code base"
msgstr "在 Python 代码库上的本地开发"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:24
msgid "Usage of https://app.readthedocs.org for open source projects"
msgstr "开源项目对 https://app.readthedocs.org 的使用"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:25
msgid ""
"Bug fixes in the code base, as it applies to running it on "
"https://app.readthedocs.org"
msgstr "代码库中与在 https://app.readthedocs.org 上运行相关的缺陷修复"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:28
msgid "Unsupported"
msgstr "不支持"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:30
msgid ""
"There are use cases that we don't support, because it doesn't further our "
"goal of promoting documentation in the open source community."
msgstr "有些使用场景我们不支持，因为这无助于推动开源社区文档发展这一目标。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:33
msgid "We do not support:"
msgstr "我们不支持："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:35
msgid "Specific usage of Sphinx and Mkdocs, that don't affect our hosting"
msgstr "不影响我们托管的 Sphinx 和 MkDocs 的特定用法"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:36
msgid "Custom installations of Read the Docs at your company"
msgstr "在你们公司定制安装 Read the Docs"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:37
msgid "Installation of Read the Docs on other platforms"
msgstr "在其他平台上安装 Read the Docs"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:38
msgid "Any installation issues outside of the Read the Docs Python Code"
msgstr "Read the Docs Python 代码之外的任何安装问题"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:41
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr "理由"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:43
msgid ""
"Read the Docs was founded to improve documentation in the open source "
"community. We fully recognize and allow the code to be used for internal "
"installs at companies, but we will not spend our time supporting it. Our "
"time is limited, and we want to spend it on the mission that we set out to "
"originally support."
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs "
"的创立初衷是改善开源社区的文档。我们完全认可并允许代码在公司内部安装使用，但不会花时间为它提供支持。我们的时间有限，希望投入到最初设定的使命上。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/open-source-philosophy.rst:49
msgid ""
"If you feel strongly about installing Read the Docs internal to a company, "
"we will happily link to third party resources on this topic. Please open an "
"issue with a proposal if you want to take on this task."
msgstr "若你坚决要在公司内部安装 Read the Docs，我们乐意提供该主题的第三方资源链接。若你想承担此任务，请提交带方案的 issue。"

